							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "{{gtMethod:name=TElixirNavigationCoder>>resolveModuleName:}} resolves aliases via `GtBridge.Analysis.resolve_alias`. {{gtMethod:name=TElixirNavigationCoder>>contextModuleName}} is the override hook — what module is being edited (nil for snippets). {{gtMethod:name=TElixirNavigationCoder>>initializeNavigationShortcuts:}} registers C-m and C-n."
						},
						{
							"__type" : "textSnippet",
							"children" : {
								"__type" : "snippets",
								"items" : [ ]
							},
							"paragraphStyle" : {
								"__type" : "textStyle"
							},
							"string" : "**Lesson learned:** an earlier version dispatched C-m through private helpers (`navigateToQualified:function:requesterObject:`, `functionDocsQueryFor:...`, `moduleDocsQuery:`) that spawned docs directly for qualified calls and only filtered for unqualified ones. The split dispatch was confusing — sometimes the user wants the implementors filter even on a qualified call (multiple arities, cross-module overrides). The trait was simplified so C-m *always* spawns the implementors filter via {{gtMethod:name=TElixirNavigationCoder>>browseImplementorsInModule:function:requesterObject:}}, and those private helpers were removed."
						}
					]
				},
